Lisa,

Our technician inspected the Raypak 2100 pool heater (Unit #2) this morning. Here's the diagnosis:

Issue: Failed ignition control module
- The electronic ignition board is not sending signal to the gas valve
- This is a known issue with Raypak 2100 units manufactured in 2022 (TSB-2023-04)
- Raypak issued a technical service bulletin and extended warranty on this component

Resolution:
- Replacement ignition module ordered (Raypak P/N 013464F)
- Expected delivery: Friday April 19th
- Installation: Monday April 22nd (2-hour service call)
- Pool should return to setpoint within 4-6 hours after repair

Cost: $0 - covered under manufacturer's extended warranty per TSB-2023-04

In the meantime, Heater Unit #1 is operating normally and can maintain the pool at approximately 78°F (below the 82°F setpoint but swimmable). I'd recommend reducing pool hours until the repair is complete to minimize heat loss.

Let me know if you need anything else.

